#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:5
#: b70a5b3eda354876a5da4c71738756c8
msgid "Crossfire and ELRS RC Systems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:7
#: 7c34807aa18746ab9763238906fa06c8
msgid "Any Crossfire/ELRS compatible receiver can be used with ArduPilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:9
#: e4b8d4f86608429ab163aae358068624
msgid "ELRS (ExpressLRS) RC systems use the CRSF protocol and are connected in a similar manner as Crossfire receivers to an autopilot UART. ELRS can also be configured to be MAVLink protocol with embedded RC control (See below). On  F4/F7 based autopilots the UART MUST be DMA enabled for reliable operation in CRSF protocol mode. Consult :ref:`common-autopilots`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:11
#: 3a533b0322994f67bef162342040ce79
msgid "If you do not wish to use telemetry then a TBS Crossfire or ELRS receiver can be connected to the **RCIN** port using :ref:`SBUS <common-rc-systems>`. You must configure the receiver to output SBUS, of course."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:15
#: 5ae2df97cf734130a0b592f6ce2ca81a
msgid "CRSF Receivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:17
#: 71df1e43bb34421bb4dcfe6d3a81f661
msgid "If you wish to use telemetry then a receiver can be connected to a UART utilizing the `CRSF <https://www.team-blacksheep.com/products/prod:crossfire_tx>`__ protocol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:19
#: a26f8582b9fb4bcf8ba5ebbad2367469
msgid "CRSF is a full-duplex protocol that supports integrated telemetry and a number of other features. Connect the RX pin of the UART to the CRSF TX pin of the CRSF device and vice versa. Currently a full-duplex UART connection is required. For best performance a UART with DMA capability on its RX port is desirable, but not required. A message will be displayed once on the GCS console, if connected to a UART without this capability on an F4/F7 based autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:22
#: c65a21e459e74d24a52e84216a36261f
msgid "In the configuration of the serial port select the RCIN protocol. So for example for serial port 4:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:24
#: a6e6481ae2544657b57ad1461280ec2b
msgid "Set :ref:`SERIAL4_PROTOCOL <SERIAL4_PROTOCOL>` = 23"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:25
#: 43f5c64fbd304f7e8ec19c38e3a50892
msgid "Set :ref:`RSSI_TYPE <RSSI_TYPE>` = 3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:27
#: 8b7695fa74714231b852e981e0308a18
msgid "The serial port baudrate is automatically set and controlled by the firmware when any serial RC protocol, such as CRSF, is detected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:29
#: 98ab536b7cc241bda0e013c602df278b
msgid "With the receiver connected and configured correctly proceed with RC calibration as normal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:31
#: babc89537b5345d9af52e24fee941555
msgid "See :ref:`common-crsf-telemetry` for information about telemetry data sent, display scripts for OpenTX transmitters, and adjustment of ArduPilot parameters via CRSF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:33
#: a209a16388c945139fc4131ab265da05
msgid "If the autopilot is rebooted via MAVLink, it will lose communication with the CRSF receiver until the receiver is power cycled. Also, the CRSF TX must be transmitting BEFORE the receiver is powered up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:36
#: 26355fc88607448e8b973b98d78fd039
msgid "MAVLink Option"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:38
#: 6dde98fdada244baa08333e63a680bda
msgid "In addition to SBUS and CRSF protocols, CRSF receivers can be configured to use MAVLink protocol for telemetry and embedded RC control. To utilize this attach to SERIAL port 4(as an example) and configure:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:40
#: ../../source/docs/common-tbs-rc.rst:56
#: 9d1271ee93d94e39b7ff5410b869b34a
#: 5304f587c8644d8fbf517183b5cc410d
msgid "Set :ref:`SERIAL4_PROTOCOL <SERIAL4_PROTOCOL>` = 2"
